{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe `external LLM (live bedrock)` job of the `Live External Integration` workflow failed on dispatch run 42939278248 (https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/42939278248, 2026-11-10 17:29 PST, main at 91182f96362). Its last green run, 42684304178 (2026-11-09, at 872e7f6c3fd), predates 06b3b1a5230 (Gerrit 3340), which moved `.github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml` to the 5.5 ids. Ticket unkempt-amaranth-archerfish needs the scheduled run (Sunday 2026-11-15 ~22:16 PST) green.\n\nFailure: `tests/external/test_structured_output_matrix.py::test_structured_output_matrix` raised `LLMInputRejectedError` wrapping pydantic-ai `ContentFilterError`: Bedrock `content_filtered`, 0 output tokens, `us.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5`.\n\n## Root cause\nMeasured live on Bedrock Opus 5.5 (us-east-1, effort high); full counts in the ROOT-CAUSE EVIDENCE comment on this ticket. The harness system prompt (\"You are a completion verifier that emits a single structured verdict.\") plus either matrix prompt asks for a ticket verdict with no criterion text and no evidence. Opus 5.5 ends the first call `content_filtered`; pydantic-ai's \"Please return text\" retry is filtered too (the CI-logged request). Single-shot as shipped 8/8 filtered, agentic 6/8; removing the system prompt 0/8; adding a concrete criterion + evidence with every other word kept 0/10 each. It is not the reasoning-in-schema refusal on epic pompous-vitriolic-macaw (text mode, no schema, no reasoning requested).\n\nProduction exposure, measured (not inferred): the real `completion-verifier` prompt (`src/rebar/llm/reviewers/completion_verifier.md`, rendered by `prompts.resolve_prompt_cached`) with a ticket context holding an AC but no evidence: Opus 5.5 0/10, Sonnet 5.5 0/10; with neither AC nor evidence: 0/10, 0/10. The empty-evidence production path is therefore not filtered at these sample sizes, and the bare system prompt above exists only in the test (`git grep -nF 'single structured verdict' -- src` returns nothing). No runtime change is in scope.\n\n## Approach\nGive the harness a verifier request with something to verify, matching what a production verifier receives. Move the system prompt and both user prompts into the pure helper `tests/external/_structured_matrix.py` (it already owns `DIRECTIVE_VARIANTS`, line 29) as `SYSTEM_PROMPT`, `AGENTIC_TRANSCRIPT_PROMPT`, `SINGLE_SHOT_PROMPT`, `PROMPTS`, so the offline oracle `tests/unit/test_structured_matrix_scorer.py` pins the whole request. Shipped text (exactly what was measured):\n- shared block: `Ticket 7c41-0d2e-9a85-b613 has one acceptance criterion: \"`add(a, b)` returns the sum of its arguments.\" Evidence: `tests/test_add.py::test_add_returns_sum` passed (1 passed in 0.01s), and `src/calc.py` defines `def add(a, b): return a + b`.`\n- agentic: the existing role line, the shared block, the existing quoted `{\"relation\": \"depends_on\", \"target_id\": \"f2f3-9cb1-335b-4e31\"}` record, then the verdict request.\n- single-shot: the shared block, then the verdict request.\n- both requests read: a JSON object with `verdict` (PASS or FAIL), a `findings` array (empty when every criterion is met), and a `summary` string.\nThe \"empty when met\" clause is needed: without it Opus 5.5 returned per-criterion findings lacking `detail`, which fail `CompletionVerdict` validation (0/20 parsed); with it 10/10 per variant parsed.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/external/_structured_matrix.py`: add the four constants.\n- `tests/external/test_structured_output_matrix.py`: use them; delete the old prompt constants.\n- `tests/unit/test_structured_matrix_scorer.py`: pin the prompt shape.\n\n## Testing\n- Unit, against string literals written in the test (not the module constants): both prompts contain the criterion sentence and the `test_add_returns_sum` evidence; labels are `agentic_transcript`, `single_shot`; `SYSTEM_PROMPT` equals the measured literal.\n- Unit, edge: the single-shot control contains no `{`; the agentic prompt contains exactly one JSON object, placed before \"emit your FINAL\", and its `target_id` differs from the verified ticket id.\n- Live, before push (recorded in a ticket comment): direct converse, 50 calls per (variant, prompt) cell, pass = 0 filtered; through the rebar runner, 5 per cell, pass = 0 filtered and every reply parses.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Root cause identified: the filtered cell and the request feature that triggers the filter, reproduced against Bedrock Opus 5.5; evidence recorded in a ticket comment.\n- [ ] Fix lands through Gerrit with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1; no new config key, env var or feature flag.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] A `Live External Integration` run on main after the fix (a manual `workflow_dispatch` run counts) shows `external LLM (live bedrock)` concluding success; run id recorded on this ticket.\n  provenance: environment=GitHub Actions Live External Integration workflow on navapbc/rebar main; principal=the CI Bedrock OIDC role (repository variable AWS_BEDROCK_CI_ROLE_ARN); privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — the criterion is about that exact workflow job, so its own run conclusion is the evidence.\n- [ ] `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN .venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/test_structured_matrix_scorer.py` passes, including the new prompt-shape tests.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0 on the pushed commit.\n"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794364429353986007,"uuid":"a9f42e20-2d8b-4a5f-bca6-64cbdc9be651"}